              "activity_type": "patch_submitted",
              "subject": "[PATCH v3 1/2] mm/mempolicy: use vm_normal_folio_pmd() in queue_folios_pmd()",
              "message_id": "20260926105110.2156652-2-gourry@gourry.net",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260926105110.2156652-2-gourry@gourry.net/",
              "date": "2026-09-26T10:51:17Z",
              "in_reply_to": null,
              "ack_type": null,
              "is_ongoing": false,
              "submitted_date": null,
              "patch_version": 3,
              "series_patch_count": null,
              "version_history": [],
              "series_items": [],
              "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a bug in the mm/mempolicy module where mbind() operations on VM_PFNMAP regions would fail due to incorrect handling of huge PMDs. The patch uses vm_normal_folio_pmd() instead of pmd_folio() to handle these cases, which also eliminates the need for separate checks for huge zero PMDs. This change allows mbind(MPOL_MF_STRICT) operations on VM_PFNMAP regions to succeed and fixes a bug that was causing crashes when trying to map MMIO BARs.",
              "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
              "review_comments": [],
              "list_id": "linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"
            },
            {
              "activity_type": "patch_submitted",
              "subject": "[PATCH v3 2/2] mm/madvise: use vm_normal_folio_pmd() in cold/pageout PMD range",
              "message_id": "20260926105110.2156652-3-gourry@gourry.net",
              "url": "https://lore.kernel.org/all/20260926105110.2156652-3-gourry@gourry.net/",
              "date": "2026-09-26T10:51:18Z",
              "in_reply_to": null,
              "ack_type": null,
              "is_ongoing": false,
              "submitted_date": null,
              "patch_version": 3,
              "series_patch_count": null,
              "version_history": [],
              "series_items": [],
              "patch_summary": "This patch fixes a bug in the madvise function where it incorrectly handles page faults for VM_MIXEDMAP regions. The issue arises when a huge PMD is inserted through vmf_insert_pfn_pmd() and then madvised with MADV_PAGEOUT. The patch uses vm_normal_folio_pmd() to validate the pfn and filter out the huge zero PMD, preventing incorrect behavior in the walker. This fix addresses a problem where the mapping carries no rmap, leading to folio_deactivate() or reclaim_pages() being called against a folio that is not owned by the mapping.",
              "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
              "review_comments": [],
              "list_id": "linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"
            }
          ],
          "patch_summary": "This patch series addresses an issue where the pmd_folio() function is called on special PMDs, which can lead to faults when reading folio fields. The patches modify two page table walkers (madvise_cold_or_pageout_pte_range and queue_folios_pmd) to use vm_normal_folio() instead of pmd_folio(), matching the behavior of their PTE halves. This change affects four callers of vmf_insert_pfn_pmd, which installs special PMDs holding raw pfns without memmap entries. The patches also introduce a behavior change for mbind(MPOL_MF_STRICT) over PMD mapped VM_PFNMAP regions, now returning 0 instead of -EIO.",
          "analysis_source": "llm-chunked-no-replies",
          "review_comments": [],
          "list_id": "linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"
        }
      ],
